      },
      "text": "**Systems Bridge:** The viral replication cycle is a pipeline with discrete stages, each a potential drug target: attachment → entry → uncoating → replication → assembly → release. Antivirals block specific pipeline stages — entry inhibitors block the handshake; polymerase inhibitors (NRTIs, NNRTIs, NS5B inhibitors) block the core replication transform; protease inhibitors block the post-translation processing step; integrase inhibitors block the write to the host genome; neuraminidase inhibitors block the release/egress step. This staging also explains why drug resistance is stage-specific: a mutation in the RT active site confers NRTI resistance without affecting entry or integration."
    },
